-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope of this license: data and models
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT License above covers the code in this repository (harness/, envs/,
train/, eval/, experiments/, scripts/, tests/, docs/ page code) and the run
logs written by it. It does not relicense third-party data or models. Those
keep the terms of their sources:

- Gemma 3 270M finetunes (exp7, checkpoints/exp7/, not committed) are Model
  Derivatives of google/gemma-3-270m-it and are subject to the Gemma Terms of
  Use and Prohibited Use Policy: https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms
- exp7 QA data (data/exp7/): items derived from ARC-Easy (allenai/ai2_arc) are
  CC BY-SA 4.0; the replay set uses Databricks Dolly-15k instructions
  (CC BY-SA 3.0) with answers generated by the base Gemma model. Arithmetic and
  country-capital items are generated.
- exp3 English corpus (data/exp3/english.txt, not committed): Wikipedia via
  the wikimedia/wikipedia dataset, CC BY-SA (and GFDL).
- exp3 romaji corpus (data/exp3/romaji.txt, not committed): romanised from
  globis-university/aozorabunko-clean, built from Aozora Bunko's public-domain
  works; see that dataset card for its terms.
- exp3 Python corpus (data/exp3/python.txt, not committed): the CPython 3.11
  standard library, under the Python Software Foundation License.
- exp3 checkpoints were trained on these corpora; treat them as derived from
  the corresponding sources.
- Atari ROMs are not included; they are provided by ale-py under its own terms.
- The original post, "Sparks of Weight-Space Programming" by Takehi, Teoh,
  Zhang and Khattab, is the work of its authors and is not covered by this
  license: https://rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-space-programming/
